invariant: INV-26
file: gcm_vaes.h
catches: test/docker-aes-runtime-qemu.sh x86-kernels
reason: gcm_vaes.h's gcm_use_vaes reads CH_CPU_VAES alone, so a key whose
  session never stated the timing of the AES instructions runs VAESENC
  and VPCLMULQDQ under a traffic key. CH_CPU_CONSTANT_TIME_AES is the one
  statement that covers the 256-bit forms (docs/decisions.md 89 and 90).
  A session's init refuses the AES suites without that bit, so no loop
  builds such a key, and the bytes are the same. bin/x86_kernels_test
  counts the calls into each kernel under every ch_cfg.cpu value, and
  test/aes-runtime-qemu.sh builds it for x86-64 and runs it under
  qemu-x86_64. The lane skips without docker, and this then reports
  unguarded rather than caught.

--- old
    return (cpu & CH_CPU_VAES) != 0 && (cpu & CH_CPU_CONSTANT_TIME_AES) != 0;
--- new
    return (cpu & CH_CPU_VAES) != 0;
